On 9/18/06, Tejun Heo <htejun@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hello, Emmanuel.
>
> Emmanuel Benisty wrote:
> > Dear Tejun,
> >
> > Thanks to your Kernel Fix for ICH7M in 2.6.18-rc7 (ata_piix: add map
> > 01b for ICH7M), I finally could get my machine to boot.
> > This machine is an ACER 5550 series with Intel 945GM Express Chipset
> > (whereas the problem has been spotted on 82801GBM/GHM). However,
> > turning DMA (on) will still give me some errors :
> >
> > hdparm -d1 /dev/sda
> >
> > /dev/sda:
> > setting using_dma to 1 (on)
> > HDIO_SET_DMA failed: Inappropriate ioctl for device
>
> That ioctl is for the old IDE and not implemented for libata.  libata
> should automatically choose the best available transfer mode.  The
> selected transfer mode is reported during initialization.  The line
> looks like the following.
>
> ata1.00: configured for UDMA/133
>
> > As this machine is different from Jonathan Dieter's one (the person
> > who spotted that problem, just for reference
> > http://www.spinics.net/lists/linux-ide/msg04732.html), please find
> > attached the lspci -n -xxx -vvv output as you requested from him (disk
> > controller card is at 00:1f.2.)
>
> So, that wasn't an isolated case.  I hope intel updates their doc soon.
>
> > Sorry to have to address this e-mail directly to you as I can imagine
> > you are very busy but this problem is quite uncommon ATM so I am
> > clueless (my skills are very basic TBH).
> >
> > Thank you very much in advance.
>
> No problem.  Just try to Cc relevant mailing list next time.
> linux-ide@vger.kernel.org is the one for ata/pata/sata stuff.  If you're
> not sure just cc linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org.
>
> --
> tejun
>

Dear Tejun,

